cluded from the accessibility tree.","repair_strategy":"Modify the syncState method to conditionally apply aria-hidden only when the menu button is visible (mobile). When the button is hidden (desktop), ensure the navigation is not hidden by setting aria-hidden=false.","edits":[{"path":"src/govuk/components/header/header.js","sha256":"33e331b7a1f44087522e90d1e295dbc0f915c8b8a82e8afd57a794d21fff4424","before":"Header.prototype.syncState = function (isVisible) {\n  this.$menuButton.classList.toggle('govuk-header__menu-button--open', isVisible)\n  this.$menuButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded', isVisible)\n  this.$menu.setAttribute('aria-hidden', !isVisible)\n}","after":"Header.prototype.syncState = function (isVisible) {\n  this.$menuButton.classList.toggle('govuk-header__menu-button--open', isVisible)\n  this.$menuButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded', isVisible)\n  if (this.$menuButton.offsetParent) {\n    // Menu button is visible (mobile)\n    this.$menu.setAttribute('aria-hidden', !isVisible);\n  } else {\n    // Menu button is hidden (desktop)\n    this.$menu.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');\n  }\n}"}],"expected_accessibility_effect":"Navigation links will be included in the accessibility tree, exposing their role as link and accessible name, allowing keyboard and screen‑reader users to reach them.","functional_risks":["If the menu button is hidden while the navigation is also visually hidden (e.g., due to custom CSS), the navigation could be incorrectly exposed to assistive technology."],"verification_requirements":["The AX assertion for #nav-apply (name \"Apply\", role \"link\") must pass after the fix.","On mobile widths, opening and closing the menu via the button must correctly toggle aria-expanded and aria-hidden on the navigation.","On desktop widths, the navigation must remain visible and not be hidden from assistive technology regardless of menu button state."]},"provenance":{"provider":"Nebius Token Factory","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b